{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconst i64 MOD1 = 998244353LL;\nconst i64 MOD2 = 1000000007LL;\nconst i64 THRESHOLD = 1000000LL;\n\ni64 N;\ni64 counter = 0, temp_counter = 0, result = 0;\nvector<i64> bucket[7];\ni64 bucket_sum[7];\n\ninline i64 normalize1(i64 x) {\n    x %= MOD1;\n    if (x < 0) x += MOD1;\n    return x;\n}\n\nvoid traverse_first(i64 level, i64 current) {\n    if (current > N) return;\n    if (level > 6) return;\n    \n    ++counter;\n    i64 adjusted = normalize1(counter - current);\n    bucket[level].push_back(adjusted);\n    bucket_sum[level] = (bucket_sum[level] + adjusted) % MOD1;\n    \n    for (i64 d = 0; d < 10; ++d) {\n        traverse_first(level + 1, current * 10 + d);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid traverse_second(i64 level, i64 current) {\n    if (current > N) return;\n    \n    if (level >= 1) {\n        if (current * THRESHOLD * 10 > N && current * THRESHOLD + THRESHOLD - 1 <= N) {\n            for (i64 i = 0, pow10 = 1; i <= 6; ++i, pow10 *= 10) {\n                i64 target = normalize1(counter - current * pow10);\n                i64 pos = lower_bound(bucket[i].begin(), bucket[i].end(), MOD1 - target) - bucket[i].begin();\n                result = (result + target * (i64)bucket[i].size() + bucket_sum[i] - MOD1 * (i64)(bucket[i].size() - pos)) % MOD2;\n            }\n            counter += temp_counter;\n            return;\n        }\n        ++counter;\n        result = (result + normalize1(counter - current)) % MOD2;\n    }\n    \n    for (i64 d = (level == 0 ? 1 : 0); d < 10; ++d) {\n        traverse_second(level + 1, current * 10 + d);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> N;\n    \n    traverse_first(0, 0);\n    temp_counter = counter;\n    counter = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= 6; ++i) {\n        sort(bucket[i].begin(), bucket[i].end());\n    }\n    \n    traverse_second(0, 0);\n    result %= MOD2;\n    if (result < 0) result += MOD2;\n    cout << result << '\\n';\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1000000)\n\nMOD1 = 998244353\nMOD2 = 1000000007\nTHRESHOLD = 1000000\n\nN = 0\ncounter = 0\ntemp_counter = 0\nresult = 0\nbucket = [[] for _ in range(7)]\nbucket_sum = [0] * 7\n\ndef normalize1(x):\n    x %= MOD1\n    if x < 0:\n        x += MOD1\n    return x\n\ndef traverse_first(level, current):\n    global counter\n    if current > N:\n        return\n    if level > 6:\n        return\n    \n    counter += 1\n    adjusted = normalize1(counter - current)\n    bucket[level].append(adjusted)\n    bucket_sum[level] = (bucket_sum[level] + adjusted) % MOD1\n    \n    for d in range(10):\n        traverse_first(level + 1, current * 10 + d)\n\ndef traverse_second(level, current):\n    global counter, result\n    if current > N:\n        return\n    \n    if level >= 1:\n        if current * THRESHOLD * 10 > N and current * THRESHOLD + THRESHOLD - 1 <= N:\n            for i in range(7):\n                pow10 = 10 ** i\n                target = normalize1(counter - current * pow10)\n                # Find position using bisect_left for lower_bound equivalent\n                pos = bisect.bisect_left(bucket[i], MOD1 - target)\n                bucket_size = len(bucket[i])\n                # Calculate the contribution\n                contribution = target * bucket_size + bucket_sum[i] - MOD1 * (bucket_size - pos)\n                result = (result + contribution) % MOD2\n            counter += temp_counter\n            return\n        counter += 1\n        result = (result + normalize1(counter - current)) % MOD2\n    \n    start_d = 1 if level == 0 else 0\n    for d in range(start_d, 10):\n        traverse_second(level + 1, current * 10 + d)\n\ndef main():\n    global N, counter, temp_counter, result, bucket, bucket_sum\n    \n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if input_data:\n        N = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Initialize\n    counter = 0\n    temp_counter = 0\n    result = 0\n    bucket = [[] for _ in range(7)]\n    bucket_sum = [0] * 7\n    \n    traverse_first(0, 0)\n    temp_counter = counter\n    counter = 0\n    \n    for i in range(7):\n        bucket[i].sort()\n    \n    traverse_second(0, 0)\n    result %= MOD2\n    if result < 0:\n        result += MOD2\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016890530241653323, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.009943829849362373, -0.11311270296573639, -0.0003815161471720785, -0.043785471469163895, -0.0011121999705210328, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.011050689965486526, -0.29507893323898315, -3.933898824470816e-06, -8.749579137656838e-05, -1.9907753085135482e-05, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0002644904307089746, -0.004101793281733